// Title: Potential DLL File Download Via PowerShell Invoke-WebRequest
// Sigma ID: 0f0450f3-8b47-441e-a31b-15a91dc243e2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Hieu Tran
// Date: 2023-03-13 | Modified: 2025-07-18
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, execution, T1059.001, T1105
// Description: Detects potential DLL files being downloaded using the PowerShell Invoke-WebRequest or Invoke-
//   RestMethod cmdlets.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.zscaler.com/blogs/security-research/onenote-growing-threat-malware-distribution
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_download_dll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "Invoke-RestMethod " or ProcessCommandLine contains "Invoke-WebRequest " or ProcessCommandLine contains "IRM " or ProcessCommandLine contains "IWR ") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "http" and ProcessCommandLine contains "OutFile" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".dll")
